# alpha-MoO3, orthorhombic layered phase.
# Fractional coordinates from Materials Project mp-20589; unit cell replaced
# with the experimental values of Kihlborg (1963): 3.9628 / 13.8550 / 3.6964 A.
#
# Do not use the MP cell as-is. MoO3 is a van der Waals layered structure and
# plain PBE overestimates the interlayer axis by ~2.7% (14.229 vs 13.855 A),
# which moves the low-angle (0k0) lines by ~0.7 deg -- enough to break the
# phase assignment. The fractional coordinates are unaffected.
#
# Kept in P1 with all 16 atoms, so structure factors are correct but no
# symmetry constraints apply: refine this phase with Cell UNCHECKED.
data_mp-20589
_cell_length_a                  3.696400
_cell_length_b                  3.962800
_cell_length_c                  13.855000
_cell_angle_alpha               90.0000
_cell_angle_beta                90.0000
_cell_angle_gamma               90.0000
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M  'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number     1
_chemical_formula_sum           'MoO3'
